{
  "note": "Manifest-driven visuals (S15, D46). The renderer asks the resolver WHAT to show; this file and the factory decide HOW. No geometry decision lives in scene.js, so swapping a procedural stand-in for a painted model later is a manifest edit rather than a renderer edit.",
  "note_tint": "`tint` names the mark token a visual takes at runtime. A visual with tint:null is fully painted and never recoloured. Meshes named \"tint\" inside a group are the only ones a tint touches \u2014 that is what keeps detection state readable without repainting the coat.",
